evaluated_feedback_rounds=len(
    completed_record_rounds & evaluated_record_rounds
),
render_rejected_experiments=render_rejected_experiments,
```

Definitions: lifecycle counts distinct checkpoint-record rounds with successful cleanup; evaluated-feedback counts those completed rounds containing an actual `status == "evaluated"` record with campaign evidence; rejected experiments count committed reserved-code invalid records even when cleanup is pending. Preserve all status/readiness/terminal rules, old summary fields, performance selection, failure taxonomy, role/token/cost counts, cleanup semantics, serialization, schema version, and historical artifacts. No changes to operations.py or other source. Do not execute records/candidates/events/wrappers/tests/models/API/evaluator/campaign, commits/push/deploy.

